        "date": "2026-11-09T23:29:29Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): an explicit M5 after a probe's tool change in every post\n\nA probe section relied on the control's tool change to stop the\nspindle. Every mill post (fanuc, haas, tormach, sinumerik, heidenhain,\nmazak) now writes its spindle-stop word - M5, MOTOFF on Mazak - after\nthe tool change and length offset, before coolant and the first move,\nwhen the section states a spindle speed of 0 (only a probe does; tools\nrefuse rpm 0). A cutting section and a legacy stream with no\nSpindleSpeed PARAM post byte-identical.\n\nGoldens: one added \"M5\" line after G43 in the four Fanuc probe goldens\n(probe_bore_centre, probe_corner, probe_corner_negative,\nprobe_edge_negative_x) and tormach/probe_guard_moves.\n\nPinned by probe_spindle_stop::{a_probe_section_stops_its_spindle_after_the_tool_change_on_every_mill_post,\na_cutting_section_states_no_spindle_stop_before_its_first_move}.\n\nFixes #574\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
